<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer — Freighthub"
  description="What Freighthub does and does not claim: editorial analysis not customs advice, ranges not quotations, no carrier relationship, no clearance guarantee."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Freighthub publishes analysis for shippers and importers. It is not a party to your shipment and
      does not act on your behalf. This page sets out what that means in practice.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial analysis, not advice</h2>
    <p>
      The content is journalism and analysis about freight, customs and certification. It is not legal,
      tax, customs or insurance advice, and it does not create a professional relationship. A customs
      classification or a certificate requirement that is right for one consignment can be wrong for
      another; the competent authority, or a licensed broker acting for you, is the source of a
      binding answer.
    </p>

    <h2>Ranges, not quotations</h2>
    <p>
      Freight rates, transit times and charges are published as ranges or as illustrative figures. They
      are not offers, and they are not a quote for your shipment. A rate that appears on this site may
      be out of date the week you read it; market conditions, fuel, capacity and season move faster
      than any static page.
    </p>

    <h2>No carrier, forwarder or broker relationship</h2>
    <p>
      Freighthub does not sell freight, book space, clear goods, insure cargo or receive commissions
      from carriers, forwarders or brokers. Where a page names a port operator or an authority, that is
      a citation, not a commercial relationship.
    </p>

    <h2>No guarantee of clearance or outcome</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing here guarantees that a consignment will clear, that a certificate will be accepted, or
      that a route will perform as described. Those outcomes depend on documents, valuation, inspection
      and the decisions of authorities that no publication controls.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Links to regulators, port operators and official documents are provided so a reader can verify a
      claim. The site does not control those pages and is not responsible for their content or
      availability.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Errors are corrected and dated. If a claim on this site is wrong, report it through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>; the process is described on
      <a href="/corrections/">corrections</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/terms/">Terms of use</a> · <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> ·
      <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>
    </p>
  </article>
